* {{IPA|en|/-siːz/|a=nonstandard, for the noun plural}}

====Usage notes====
The nonstandard pronunciation {{IPAchar|/ˈpɹɒsɛˌsiːz/}} (with the final syllable pronounced like {{m|en|seize}}) is a [[hypercorrection]] due to plurals like {{m|en|parentheses}} and {{m|en|hypotheses}} from Ancient Greek. Compare {{m|en|biases}} and {{m|en|premises}}, where a similar influence is sometimes found.

